 in Franklin County has come in under 90% of normal in June to July in 34 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September on the middle of the grids came in at 52% of normal, and July to August at 66%. So far in 2026, May to June on the middle of the grids stands at 154% of normal. Grid 29629 had its driest year in 1956 at 71%, and its preliminary August to September 2026 estimate sits at 70.2.</p>"}
